i2c-display (0.7.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * BREAKING: the daemon now exits with status 1 when the display hardware
    cannot be initialised instead of falling back to a mock display, which
    made bus, permission and config failures look like rendering bugs; use
    -mock explicitly without hardware. The systemd unit adds
    StartLimitIntervalSec/StartLimitBurst so a missing panel stops retrying
  * Text no longer truncates off the right edge of 128-wide panels: pages use
    the compact 5x7 font before truncating, so IPv4 addresses and all three
    load averages are shown; load label and disk/memory formats trimmed to fit
  * MockDisplay.DrawImage now thresholds on the brightest channel like the
    SSD1306/SH1106 drivers, so green/red/yellow text renders in tests
  * Packaging: make dist writes i2c-display-<version>-vendored.tar.gz instead
    of reusing the plain source tarball name; both archives now come from one
    git archive of the tag (new make dist-src), deb/deb-src vendor automatically

 -- Dennis Gilmore <dennis@ausil.us>  Fri, 13 Nov 2026 20:25:04 -0600

